Changes made in this fork
--------------------------

Alejandro Buján's work, carried over: the rope, the clothespin, the glass, and
the way a card swings when it lands on the line.

Written for Clothespeg:

- The data model. A card stores the contents rather than a path to a file, so
  text and images can be hung on the line at all, and copied without the
  original having to exist any more.
- A second rope for notes, written rather than copied, with rows that can be
  ticked off and a paper that scrolls.
- The pill on the line: a filter, a search, the page counter, dates, and the
  prop toggle.
- Watching — pinning a card so it stays on the line — and hiding.
- The screenshot inbox, opt-in, off by default.
- A line that can be paged without a trackpad: the wheel, a hold on the
  arrows, and the mouse's thumb keys behind a switch. A two-finger swipe over
  the empty part of the line works now, which it did not before.
- Accent colours drawn from the wallpaper, and a light/dark reading that
  follows the system.
